2. Authorises the member states of the African Union to deploy up to the authorised troop and police ceilings established for AUSSOM, in full agreement and with the explicit consent of the Federal Government of Somalia, through bilateral agreements, in full respect of Somalia's sovereignty and territorial integrity, to support the phased transfer of security responsibilities to the Somali security forces;

3. Calls upon AUSSOM and the Somali National Army to enhance joint planning and operational coordination in offensive operations against Al-Shabaab, to consolidate territorial control, secure main supply routes, and create enabling conditions for civilian-led stabilisation and governance;

4. Requests the Secretary-General to continue to provide logistical support through UNSOS, on a reimbursable and cost-recovery basis where applicable, to AUSSOM and to endorsed Somali security forces engaged in joint operations with AUSSOM, within the parameters authorised in relevant Council resolutions, encourages UNSOS to explore options to enhance logistical support to endorsed Somali security forces taking over frontline responsibilities from AUSSOM, and encourages UNSOS to expand procurement from the local Somali market wherever feasible, in order to support Somalia's socioeconomic recovery and capacity-building;

