6. Urges the African Union and troop- and police-contributing countries to ensure that all AUSSOM operations comply strictly with international humanitarian law and international human rights law, including through the full application of the United Nations Human Rights Due Diligence Policy (HRDDP) and the AU Strategic Framework for Compliance and Accountability, and to maintain robust mechanisms for child protection and the prevention of, and response to, civilian harm;

7. Encourages the Federal Government of Somalia to accelerate the generation, training, and integration of capable, accountable, and affordable national security forces, in line with the SSDP, to enable the timely and sustainable drawdown and eventual exit of international forces;

